  "verdict": "With the rest of the dome at α 0.50 and the window at α_c 1.00 (the bound), the capsule's hottest hour stays under the 70 °C EDLC rating for every named window — at most 58.9 °C (61.8 °C with h_c × 0.7). The cambium under the flange's thinnest contact stays under its 50 °C gate in full sun and still air for one_package_in_the_crown_KXOB25-07X1TF, four_dies_in_the_crown_XOD17-04B, flat_crown_circle; it does not clear it for bore_circle. On the bound the largest dark aperture that keeps it under is ≈ 3.67 cm² (grid 0.10 cm²). Every number is an UPPER bound inherited from 71 and 78.",
  "not_seen": [
    "the window's optics — transmittance, its own absorption, the cavity's greenhouse (isothermal lump)",
    "a cell's real absorptance (α_c 0.90 is ours)",
    "71 takes the crown as a flat disc of the dome's diameter: a window wider than the flat crown sits on the curved R5 edge, whose projection this construction does not follow",
    "whether a window meets the ratified α ≤ 0.5 — a verdict, not a number",
    "the RF half of the window (01_03 §4)",
    "every ceiling of 71 and 78 (sunlit bark, ERA5 smoothing, 1D, adiabatic ends)"
  ]
}
